This Confidentiality and Non‑Disclosure Agreement (“Agreement”) is made between Kahana Inc. (“Kahana”) and the undersigned individual or entity (“Recipient”).

1. Purpose
In connection with Recipient’s relationship with Kahana (as an employee, contractor, advisor, prospective partner, or other role), Recipient may receive or access certain non‑public information about Kahana, its customers, users, partners, or vendors (“Confidential Information”). The purpose of this Agreement is to protect that information.

2. Definition of Confidential Information
“Confidential Information” means any non‑public information disclosed or made available to Recipient, directly or indirectly, in any form, including but not limited to:

Technical information (software, source code, system designs, architecture, infrastructure details).

Business information (roadmaps, financials, pricing, customer lists, marketing plans, strategies).

Customer and user information (workspaces, content, usage data, contact details, support communications).

Security and operational information (security controls, incidents, internal processes and documentation).

Confidential Information does not include information that Recipient can demonstrate:

Is or becomes publicly available through no fault or action of Recipient.

Was lawfully known to Recipient before disclosure by Kahana, without a duty of confidentiality.

Is independently developed by Recipient without use of Kahana’s Confidential Information.

Is received lawfully from a third party without a duty of confidentiality.

3. Obligations of Recipient
Recipient agrees to:

Use Confidential Information solely for legitimate business purposes related to Recipient’s role with Kahana.

Not disclose Confidential Information to any third party without Kahana’s prior written consent, except to Recipient’s own employees or contractors who need to know it for the same purpose and are bound by similar confidentiality obligations.

Protect Confidential Information with at least reasonable care and no less than the care used to protect Recipient’s own confidential information.

Not copy, store, or transfer Confidential Information to personal accounts, devices, or storage services except as explicitly authorized by Kahana policies.

Immediately notify Kahana if Recipient becomes aware of any unauthorized use, access, or disclosure of Confidential Information.

4. Security and Data Protection
Recipient will follow all applicable Kahana policies regarding security, acceptable use, data handling, and incident reporting. This includes:

Using only authorized systems and tools for work involving Kahana data.

Protecting accounts and devices with strong authentication and access controls.

Promptly reporting any suspected security incident or data exposure to Kahana.

5. Required Disclosures
If Recipient is required by law, regulation, or court order to disclose any Confidential Information:

Recipient will, to the extent legally permitted, promptly notify Kahana so Kahana may seek protective measures.

Recipient will disclose only the portion of Confidential Information that is legally required and will use reasonable efforts to ensure it remains protected.

6. Ownership and No License
All Confidential Information remains the property of Kahana or its customers, as applicable. No license or rights to Kahana’s intellectual property are granted under this Agreement except the limited right to use Confidential Information for the permitted purpose described above.

7. Term and Survival
This Agreement becomes effective on the date signed by Recipient and continues for the duration of Recipient’s relationship with Kahana.

Recipient’s obligations to protect Confidential Information:

Apply during the relationship; and

Survive termination of the relationship for a period of at least three (3) years, or longer if required by law or contract, except for trade secrets and customer data, which must be protected for as long as they remain non‑public.

8. Return or Destruction of Information
Upon Kahana’s request or upon termination of Recipient’s relationship with Kahana (whichever occurs first), Recipient will:

Return or, at Kahana’s direction, securely destroy all Confidential Information in Recipient’s possession or control, regardless of medium, except for copies retained only as required by law.

Confirm completion of such return or destruction if requested by Kahana.

9. Remedies
Recipient acknowledges that unauthorized disclosure or use of Confidential Information may cause irreparable harm to Kahana and/or its customers, for which monetary damages may be inadequate. Kahana may seek injunctive relief and other appropriate remedies in addition to any other rights it may have at law or in equity.

10. General
This Agreement does not create an employment contract or guarantee of continued engagement.

If any provision of this Agreement is held invalid or unenforceable, the remaining provisions will continue in full force and effect.

